@startuml seq_scan_analysis
' DermaTrack — Scan capture -> analysis -> severity result
' (the "patient uploads skin image -> graded" flow; there is no human "diagnosis").
' From camera_screen / scan_session -> scan_service -> Storage -> analyze-scan edge fn
' -> Roboflow + Hugging Face -> scans row -> scan_detail_screen.
autonumber
actor Patient
participant "Camera /\nScanSession" as UI
participant "ScanService" as SS
participant "Supabase Storage\n(scan-images)" as ST
participant "analyze-scan\n(Edge Function)" as EF
participant "Roboflow" as RB
participant "Hugging Face" as HF
database "scans" as DB
participant "ScanDetailScreen" as RES

Patient -> UI : capture / pick image (region)
UI -> SS : submitScan(bytes, region, sessionId)
SS -> ST : upload {user_id}/{scan_id}.jpg
ST --> SS : ok
SS -> EF : invoke(scan_id, image_path, region, face_bbox)
EF -> RB : detect lesions
RB --> EF : predictions (classes, bboxes)
EF -> HF : classify severity (skintelligent)
HF --> EF : level / confidence
EF -> EF : combine -> Cook grade + severity_label
EF -> DB : insert scans row (counts, lesions, metadata)
DB --> EF : row
EF --> SS : { scan }
SS --> UI : Scan (prepended to in-memory list)
UI -> RES : open result
RES -> RES : SeverityGuidance.fromScan() -> Mild/Moderate/Severe + guidance
RES --> Patient : severity + guidance + non-diagnostic disclaimer

note over EF
  20s AbortController around HF; 45s overall invoke timeout.
  Soft-fails to Roboflow-only if HF is unavailable.
end note
@enduml
